{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"eb3b2b36520317b1","name":"card_event_way_of_subjects","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Homefront/events/card_event_way_of_subjects","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"WAY OF SUBJECTS","text":"All Japanese cards in your deck get Bond and \"Your HQ gets +1 defense when you play this card.\"","flavorText":"Shinmin no Michi (The Way of Subjects) was a political guide published by Japan’s Ministry of Education in 1941. It was used in schools and the military to promote loyalty to the Emperor and support for Japan’s war efforts. The text claimed Japan was a divine nation with a duty to lead Asia and resist Western influence. It rejected ideas like liberalism, communism and individualism, calling them dangerous to national unity. Instead, it taught that people should obey the Emperor, respect their parents, and put the nation above themselves. The message was clear: every citizen’s role was to serve the Emperor and the country without question. Shinmin no Michi was a key part of Japan’s wartime propaganda, used to shape public thinking and justify military expansion during WWII.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_way_of_subjects","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_way_of_subjects_title","SourceString":"WAY OF SUBJECTS","LocalizedString":"WAY OF SUBJECTS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_way_of_subjects_text","SourceString":"All Japanese cards in your deck get Bond and \"Your HQ gets +1 defense when you play this card.\"","LocalizedString":"All Japanese cards in your deck get Bond and \"Your HQ gets +1 defense when you play this card.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_way_of_subjects_history","SourceString":"Shinmin no Michi (The Way of Subjects) was a political guide published by Japan’s Ministry of Education in 1941. It was used in schools and the military to promote loyalty to the Emperor and support for Japan’s war efforts. The text claimed Japan was a divine nation with a duty to lead Asia and resist Western influence. It rejected ideas like liberalism, communism and individualism, calling them dangerous to national unity. Instead, it taught that people should obey the Emperor, respect their parents, and put the nation above themselves. The message was clear: every citizen’s role was to serve the Emperor and the country without question. Shinmin no Michi was a key part of Japan’s wartime propaganda, used to shape public thinking and justify military expansion during WWII.","LocalizedString":"Shinmin no Michi (The Way of Subjects) was a political guide published by Japan’s Ministry of Education in 1941. It was used in schools and the military to promote loyalty to the Emperor and support for Japan’s war efforts. The text claimed Japan was a divine nation with a duty to lead Asia and resist Western influence. It rejected ideas like liberalism, communism and individualism, calling them dangerous to national unity. Instead, it taught that people should obey the Emperor, respect their parents, and put the nation above themselves. The message was clear: every citizen’s role was to serve the Emperor and the country without question. Shinmin no Michi was a key part of Japan’s wartime propaganda, used to shape public thinking and justify military expansion during WWII."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/10_Homefront/T_way_of_subjects.T_way_of_subjects","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"As